<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="LadyBird-C-Theme" spTempo="240">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1939 (written; released in 1948)
Composer:	Tadd Dameron
Lyricist:	Stanley Cornfield (lyrics added later; often performed instrumentally)
Form:	16-bar AABC
Style:	Bebop; medium swing
Key:	C major

Dameron wrote “Lady Bird” around 1939, and it was released in
1948; it became a widely played bebop standard. Its compact
16-bar form and shifting harmonies are characteristic of
Dameron’s writing.</spComments>
